If inject probe, candidate detection still uses PATH entries from env and cwd. Tests can use fake cwd and env PATH.

But dedupe candidates: if env PATH includes a temp dir with fake opencode and local fake. Fine.

For `probe` injection, easier test. In default probe use spawnSync. In tests injection by path mapping returns results.

Note `execFileSync` may throw when binary outputs to stderr or exit non-zero. Good.

Potential issue: running `--version` on a global OpenCode v1 could produce `opencode 0.x`; we skip incompatible. Good.

What about global path includes `/snap/bin/opencode` inaccessible? access? probe returns EACCES -> permission diag then continue. Fine.

Need not run version probe when platform unsupported? Return early, no. This avoids executing wrong binaries under Rosetta.

