Check `inline.getBoundingClientRect().width <= 22ch approx`? The CSS max-width 22ch. We can assert `inline.scrollWidth > inline.clientWidth && getComputedStyle(inline).textOverflow === "ellipsis"` (ellipsis). For prose/markdown, assert `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth` after appending? The host fixed width 320px and overflow-wrap anywhere, so should not overflow. Compute `host.scrollWidth <= 320+1`. But prose has white-space pre-wrap, overflow-wrap anywhere; okay.
